+// Brain Engine 0109 (LLAMA_MOE_REGISTER_RAM=1, off unless set): the brain map's expert tensors that stay in RAM are
+// registered with the card (pinned in place), up to a RAM budget, so every upload from them is a real asynchronous copy
+// at the link's speed instead of one staged through the driver's small buffer. Lossless: the same bytes go up.
+// open() at context start, close() when it goes (after the cards finished); registered() says whether [p, p + n) lies
+// wholly in registered memory (any thread). The registry is shared by every context of the same brain.
+void llama_ram_register_open(const llama_model & model, const std::vector<ggml_backend_t> & backends);
+void llama_ram_register_close(const llama_model & model, const std::vector<ggml_backend_t> & backends);
+bool llama_ram_registered(const void * p, size_t n);
